%% Agent Relay self-hosted: the main request flows through the deployed suite.
%% Source of truth for agent-relay-request-flow.svg / .png (mermaid-cli 11.4.2,
%% -b white, PNG at -s 2). Client calls cross the GKE HTTPS load balancer.
%% Service-to-service calls stay in-cluster: relay-cloud-api to the read API,
%% and the ingest edge to relay-cloud-api for token introspection. History is
%% native (read API + ingest edge on the history host); no RelayAuth.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User as Team member (browser)
  participant Desktop as Agent Relay Desktop
  participant Dash as relay-dashboard<br/>(dashboard host)
  participant API as relay-cloud-api<br/>(api host, /cloud/api)
  participant Ingest as ingest edge<br/>(history host)
  participant Hist as read API<br/>(history host)
  participant Cast as relaycast<br/>(cast host)
  participant Agent as CLI / SDK agent
  participant Peer as Peer agent

  rect rgb(238, 242, 255)
    Note over Desktop,API: 1. Desktop sign-in with device approval
    Desktop->>API: start device authorization (custom deployment origin)
    API-->>Desktop: device code + verification URL
    User->>Dash: open verification URL, sign in
    Dash->>API: approve device for org / workspace
    Desktop->>API: poll for the device token
    API-->>Desktop: session + scoped Relaycast and History credentials
  end

  rect rgb(236, 253, 245)
    Note over Desktop,Ingest: 2. Session upload (durable delivery batches)
    Desktop->>Ingest: POST delivery batch (scoped token)
    Ingest->>API: introspect token
    Ingest-->>Desktop: accepted (retries are idempotent)
    Note right of Ingest: stored in the Sessions Pipeline (hoopdb + object storage)
  end

  rect rgb(240, 249, 255)
    Note over User,Hist: 3. Dashboard read
    User->>Dash: open Sessions
    Dash->>API: GET sessions (same-origin /cloud/api)
    API->>Hist: list / replay / search for the workspace
    Hist-->>API: workspace-scoped results
    API-->>Dash: sessions
  end

  rect rgb(255, 247, 237)
    Note over Cast,Peer: 4. Agent messaging
    Agent->>Cast: register + connect /v1/node/ws (workspace credential)
    Peer->>Cast: register + connect /v1/node/ws
    Agent->>Cast: send message to a peer or channel
    Cast-->>Peer: deliver over the peer's socket
    Peer->>Cast: reply in the same conversation
    Cast-->>Agent: deliver the reply
    Note over Cast: /internal and /v1/workspaces are denied at the edge
  end
